  "body": "Varying helper gauges can remain nonzero while a recursive child or residual wrapper runs. This package imposes **gauge zero at every non-scalar boundary**, prices that restriction exactly, and admits representative complete words to the retained local scalar/frame/wrapper checker. **Finite scalar construction and exact boundary-price comparison; no new kappa.**\n\nSagar Thakrar's concurrent **#1259** already supplies varying gauges and the clipping/shortest-path mechanism, independently rediscovered during this work. That overlap is credited prominently. The added result is the stricter boundary contract, its exact cost, wrapped-helper coverage and local admission evidence\u2014not priority for varying gauges.\n\n- All 32 pinned #1259 unrestricted minima reproduce exactly. Resetting at every non-scalar event costs **4 real primitives per complex call** at L276 and L427, and zero at L359. The restriction therefore has a measured exact price and avoids *new* nonzero-gauge commutation through children/wrappers.\n- Exhaustive exact optimization over all **477** no-COPY/clear helpers and all integer exponents gives L427: **522** primitives saved per complex call in each orientation. The proof clips to a finite interval without assuming an empirical cutoff.\n- The domain includes **240 wrapped helpers**, excluded by #1259. The best wrapped witness, L652, saves **72** and passes complete local scalar/frame/wrapper admission in both orientations.\n- Adding a zero-boundary L359 schedule to the *fixed* #1214 two-helper word saves **518 extra**, for **1,094 total**: 149,002\u2192147,908 forward and 149,018\u2192147,924 backward. Its zero-boundary contract is relative to that fixed predecessor word; #1214's constant gauges and their inherited assumptions remain. This is not a joint three-helper optimum.\n\n#1263 has the larger 13,000 saving with many constant gauges. No best bill across classes or composition with #1263/#1170 is claimed. Paid recursive profiles and 52/68-bit positive local envelopes remain unchanged under the inherited 192-bit allowance. No selected-frontier or upstream file changes.\n\n## Reproduce and evidence\n\n```sh\npython3 -I -B research/k8-phase-local-gauges/reproduce.py\n```\n\nExpected final marker: `PASS_COMPLETE_K8_PHASE_LOCAL_GAUGES`.\n\n- Separate distance-transform DP uses literal PR696 lowerer prices: **1,910 minima**, **759,448 padded vertices**, all agree.\n- Six complete literal words: **445,342 primitives**, all **713** initial columns including dirty coefficient work. Macro replays separately check all 712 original columns.\n- Three complete variants pass the unchanged source-pinned local frame/wrapper checker, **25 inherited mutation controls each**.\n- Ten package test groups, including 258 exhaustive tiny path problems; four additional predecessor-price/coverage controls; normal/optimized isolated checks; complete offline Python 3.12.13 replay from a path containing spaces; 25 selected-record tests and integrity pass.\n\nFull native C++ compiler, hosted/global/controller admission, outer repricing, selected cold replay, remote CI and Lean were not run. All-size, realization, hosting, precision/tape, analytic and bit assumptions remain. Written clipping/telescoping arguments and finite exact checks do not formalize the multiplication theorem.\n\nBase `dadfea6e8a78ff6ba901705f87532a71c6f5bbb8`, OS-random seed26, original complex-supplier track. Source pins include #1161 `d210969d3158a1e6c505e41f67dd84e555c88564`, #1214 `26162c56ec9c50a80e49949f36d4dd9a137a76a6`, and #1259 `61367611154266a982fe25e1a6243a8aad77227d`. Final broad gauge-overlap refresh covered860 open PR bodies through #1268. No pinned sprint issue existed; the local claim and final refinement are preserved.\n\nCredit @woklerx, Hanson Sun/@bbMisk, Sagar Thakrar, icekylinx, Jeremy Kothe, Rohan Arun, Hao Yan, Douglas Colkitt and the retained supplier lineage. Prepared for **Philipp/@mightyOil** with substantial **OpenAI Codex/GPT-6 Astra** assistance in mathematics, code and writing. Both separate implementations are AI-assisted; no independent human review is claimed. Apache-2.0; original notices retained. Concrete next questions are in the README.\n",
